WEBVTT

00:00:03.680 --> 00:00:10.260
Wildlife Unlimited Foundation seeks to instill a love for animals with education and through environmental awareness.

00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:20.820
On land and underwater, sportsman and photographer, Bill Porter with son John and family.

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:30.000
Invite you all to join them at a spot in the country where we hope to see some wildlife still run free.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.760
We'll go hunting, climbing, fishing, diving,

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:36.800
see things that help to set the spirit free.

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:42.300
We might take some of the surplus that the good Lord has provided,

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:46.300
always mindful of the sportsman's creed.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:49.940
So the wildlife we all love remains unlimited.

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:55.510
Oh, Bill and Rose and little John, who's grown to be a man,

00:00:55.800 --> 00:01:00.000
will show you through a camera's eye, wonders of glance.

00:01:01.180 --> 00:01:08.450
might camp with them by mountain streets or run barefoot in the sand but where you go recall the

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:17.410
creed keep the wildlife unlimited not so very far away in a place we would all love to live in

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:23.280
lives a man in tune with nature a man who is tolerated by the wild ones

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:29.730
he lives in the big woods with them he makes no pets just observes and enjoys

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:37.640
sportsman's more than just a hunter or a fisherman. There's things to see to all the minds of many

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:46.340
immortal men. From the way the wild protect their young to canyons carved in sand. Oh don't take

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:54.340
them all as you recall. We're for wildlife unlimited. Man of the woods has told me a lot

00:01:54.340 --> 00:02:00.000
of stories and taught me a lot about how to live in harmony with the wild ones. Like this

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:06.210
story about thunder the black wolf the first time he ever saw the black wolf it

00:02:06.210 --> 00:02:11.060
was threatening to rain thunderheads were rolling in and the earth trembled

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:13.030
with their mighty roar

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:55.730
lightning flashed across the sky.

00:03:02.650 --> 00:03:08.280
And there she was, as black as night, fighting with that log, with all the fury of the storm.

00:03:09.160 --> 00:03:11.560
And so she got her name, Thunder.

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:22.620
Probably it was only his imagination, but it seemed like every time he saw her after that, he could hear the thunder roll.

00:03:57.260 --> 00:04:00.000
The old man always took the time to stop

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.990
and examine the flowers.

00:04:01.990 --> 00:04:06.880
He liked all of them, from the bouncing beds to the lobellas.

00:05:15.520 --> 00:05:20.830
We found that the lobellis down by the crypt banks were more flowered out this time of

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:22.450
year.

00:05:22.450 --> 00:05:23.400
What a place to be.

00:05:33.390 --> 00:05:37.390
The second time he saw her, it was about to storm again.

00:05:37.390 --> 00:05:40.080
This time she was hunting in an old meadow

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:44.470
that was growing up in young pines and briars.

00:05:44.470 --> 00:05:47.480
And the colors stood out so bright just before the storm.

00:06:25.470 --> 00:06:30.000
told me about the many times that he had seen her high in the hills under the

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.330
overhanging rocks and always hunting.

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:56.220
one time she almost came up to him but not quite many times he had seen her on the top of standing

00:07:56.220 --> 00:08:00.000
rock as he called it or on the nearby

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:21.500
ledge surveying her kingdom like a queen from her tower also other wolves in the area like the pack

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:28.930
of gray timber wolves the old man didn't see much of them unless he passed by their den in the spring

00:08:35.660 --> 00:08:39.230
- Wolves live in packs far from civilization

00:08:39.230 --> 00:08:41.570
and are very rarely seen at all.

00:08:41.570 --> 00:08:45.110
So the old man always considered this an exceptional treat.

00:09:58.800 --> 00:09:59.920
One summer day.

00:10:00.060 --> 00:10:05.020
Two of the Timberwolf cubs were trying out their new hunting skills down by the cold

00:10:05.020 --> 00:10:05.990
trout stream.

00:11:04.600 --> 00:11:11.780
one hot sunny afternoon more tired than hungry the old man fell asleep in the warm afternoon sun

00:11:11.780 --> 00:11:15.780
and was totally unaware of the guests that dropped in for lunch

00:14:50.990 --> 00:14:56.310
One time that really stands out in my mind is the time that Thunder was hunting for pheasants.

00:14:57.190 --> 00:15:00.000
Down along the edge of the woods were the birds.

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.440
Friars grew out into the grassy fields.

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:46.710
The animals were not as wary of the old man as other people, so they came in real close

00:15:46.710 --> 00:15:52.070
to him, like the time he had been out on a sunny but cold winter day, and the wind had

00:15:52.070 --> 00:15:57.590
made it feel a lot colder, so the old man made a fire on the banks of a small frozen

00:15:57.590 --> 00:15:57.910
lake.

00:15:59.530 --> 00:16:00.000
It wasn't.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:04.200
long until he noticed a deer standing off to his left,

00:16:04.200 --> 00:16:06.150
just watching the fox and him.

00:16:36.910 --> 00:16:43.700
The fox he knew as Swamp Fox came in for a closer look at the fire, then found the remains of a dead deer.

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:28.930
The swamp fox was so excited, then hurried off to get her meat.

00:17:34.760 --> 00:17:35.480
Thank you.

00:18:47.020 --> 00:18:55.200
It was after they had returned that the old man had a chance to see two foxes fight, an unusual fight, to say the least.

00:20:17.310 --> 00:20:19.310
The old man had watched the Swamp Fox

00:20:19.310 --> 00:20:22.140
after a squirrel in a stump.

00:20:22.140 --> 00:20:24.030
He called her Swamp Fox

00:20:24.030 --> 00:20:26.250
because almost every time he saw her,

00:20:26.250 --> 00:20:29.540
she was down by the swamp or on the edge of a lake.

00:20:54.220 --> 00:21:00.000
day by the fire, the deer and the fox all but ignored each other. But on a different day,

00:21:00.860 --> 00:21:04.450
in a different place, it was a different story.

00:22:00.350 --> 00:22:02.510
The old man seen thunder in the winter, too.

00:22:03.450 --> 00:22:06.250
One time, he was rubbing on a tree that had fell down.

00:22:08.250 --> 00:22:12.190
Wolves do this, rub the scent of something else on themselves,

00:22:12.640 --> 00:22:15.870
to hide the scent of their own odor from their prey.

00:22:17.140 --> 00:22:19.120
Well, this time, he didn't need to hide it.

00:22:19.320 --> 00:22:25.160
For under the tree was the remains of a deer thunder had returned to eat more of.

00:22:56.840 --> 00:22:59.600
Once in a while, when the snow wasn't too deep,

00:23:00.030 --> 00:23:04.910
Or when he just had an urge to do so, the old man would go back up to Stand Rock.

00:23:05.780 --> 00:23:12.650
And yes, once in a while, there he'd see thunder at her favorite spot, surveying her kingdom.

00:23:33.960 --> 00:23:40.200
One cold winter day, the old man started out early to check on a bear den he had seen earlier.

00:23:40.200 --> 00:23:46.000
He was anxious to see if the sow inside had had her cubs, and just how many.

00:24:40.400 --> 00:24:43.810
There she was, snug inside, and there were the cubs.

00:24:44.920 --> 00:24:50.310
One, two of them, she said.

00:24:51.460 --> 00:24:53.080
It would be a happy walk home.

00:25:03.160 --> 00:25:24.850
Things change, and this time it was the weather.

00:25:26.150 --> 00:25:30.000
For long, the wind had picked up, and it had started to snow.

00:25:33.390 --> 00:25:41.760
The old man knew to keep on moving, but even as experienced as he was, he knew he'd be lucky to find his way out.

00:25:43.520 --> 00:25:45.620
Then he thought he heard the cry of a wolf.

00:26:05.560 --> 00:26:08.100
It was definitely the cry of the wolf.

00:26:08.740 --> 00:26:14.160
Don't usually howl in a snowstorm, but the old man headed for the sound anyway.

00:26:14.820 --> 00:26:17.100
He knew the wolf would be headed for cover, too.

00:26:18.360 --> 00:26:21.220
He soon found the tracks and buried along them.

00:26:23.220 --> 00:26:25.560
They'd soon be blown in if he didn't keep up.

00:26:27.090 --> 00:26:29.110
After a while, he recognized the area.

00:26:30.160 --> 00:26:31.880
It was the clearing by his cabin.

00:26:33.550 --> 00:26:37.870
Had it been luck, or had it been thunder helping out an old friend?

00:26:38.170 --> 00:26:43.910
We'll never know for sure, but I know one old man that still loves the sound of thunder.

00:26:48.580 --> 00:26:52.260
There are many other stories centering around the old man of the woods available.

00:26:53.070 --> 00:26:58.490
Victory the Bear has the old man recalling a story about how he helped the baby bear.

00:27:00.090 --> 00:27:01.470
Their health came in return.

00:27:03.010 --> 00:27:23.220
This is a place of beauty and mystic wonders.

00:27:30.700 --> 00:27:36.250
A smallmouth bass called old Gertrude follows the nesting and raising habits of the young.

00:27:36.560 --> 00:27:42.480
Stag, the story of a white-tailed buck, is all about the yearly development of the white-tailed year.

